tence  right or why like why didn't they why  didn't they use that right why didn't  they use eternity and what a lot of  people are seeing this as and honestly i  think it's a legitimate beef that i  think that the marvel cinematic universe  is really going to run the problems with  this if they're not careful people are  starting to see it as this ongoing use  of mcguffins that what you have here are  writers and directors who are creating  stories and they don't know how to end  them and so what they're doing is just  quite literally pulling random stuff out  of their ass and then just saying well  what if gore goes to eternity  and just wishes his daughter back and  then not giving any real thought to the  question in the greater scheme of  everything that's happened in the mcu  how is this going to affect it because  now people are kind of people are  literally asking these questions like  why why did they do that before why  didn't thor do that before why did the  avengers go through all that what all  thor had to do was like hey wait a  minute guys everybody relax everybody  chill i know things are pretty bad but  here's the thing so so out in the  dimension of manifestations right  there's this dude that just sits around  all day long doing literally nothing  and and it's really a statue more than  anything else that basically looks like  the universe and because i have storm  breaker now we can just go there and  just wish for everything to be undone  and for everything to go back to the way  it was before we can just wish for that  i mean you guys want to do that right i  feel like they all look around and  captain america would be like uh  yeah man  let's do that because trying to figure  out time travel  and then going back into the past  and taking the infinity stones out of  particular locations and how to make  sure we put them back in the exact  locations and all that stuff kind of  seems a little bit unnecessary if all we  have to do is just go to that guy and  ask him to fix everything right like  it's i i totally understand where people  are coming from and this use of  mcguffins in a lot of ways just kind of  seems to be getting out of hand i  wouldn't say that like taika watiti and  those guys are lazy writers and and lazy  directors but what i am saying is the  use of mcguffins in the mcu  kind of feels like it's getting to that  point and and so i certainly see where a  lot of people are just sort of like this  like something needs to be done about  this now what it also does here though  is it does introduce some interesting  possibilities for example gore's  daughter with her like reflection and  everything could potentially be the  universe's stand-in for captain universe  or possibly even cubic and the reason  why is because when she comes back she's  got that whole godly type look right  like that whole that whole like looking  like like the reflection of the universe  eternity that kind of a thing and so for  a while i've suspected that the marvel  cinematic universe is going to try to  find a way to introduce captain universe  and the nature of captain universe is  that it was a being that was designed to  safeguard the universe from various  threats that exist out there and that  with gore having done everything he's  done and if we look at the marvel  cinematic universe phase 4 and thor 4 as  a world building film how far of of of  outside the realm of possibility do you  think it is that gore's actions woke up  null and that if it's true nola's on his  way here and if that's the case eternity  would be aware of it at the very least i  don't we don't know it's any anything  behind its motivations or anything like  that then it basically turns the  daughter of gore into captain universe  and she just goes forward from there i  don't really think she'd be like a cubic  those of you guys who don't know cubic  was basically a sentient cosmic cube  well there were a couple of them there  was kobach way back in the day then  there's cubic which is the more recent  one and i don't really think that's the  case i don't think we're getting like a  like a like you know the daughter of  thor of gore coming back is what's  effectively a cosmic cube channeling the  energy of the beyond verse right or the  energy of eternity or something along  those lines i think it's more reasonable  she would be a captain universe type  character i think that'd be awesome if  that was the case don't necessarily know  if it is but the other thing about this  is that zeus saying that the gods are a  joke of course is likely a reference to  this film  at least this film series of thor  becoming more successful when they  started leaning into more of the jokey  style but again i i feel like it's kind  of wearing out i think it's kind of  wearing a little thin people like okay  look i mean thor being funny was great  for like a movie or so but like we kind  of want serious throwback but i don't i  don't know if we're going to get that  again you know i'm kind of i'm sort of  split i like the comedy element but i  also kind of miss the serious element  right now here's one of the other cool  things too here is that valhalla is a  real place that actually exists which  makes sense given the nature of the thor  mythos and like omnipotent city and all  those places actually exist but that  basically means that the death of almost  any asgardian god and really any god in  general could be made meaningless and  that marvel will probably use this fact  at least at some point to shake up  things by bringing certain characters  back to life so that's cool i love the  idea of valhalla now what this means is  that likely jane foster will go on there  they may bring her back as some  variation of thor later on i wouldn't be  surprised if valkyrie as she exists in  the mcu will end up becoming jane foster  i mean we know that valkyrie is alive  right like she and sif and them are like  training the kids in asgard and so on  and so forth so jane foster is kind of  adamant the only reason i even go with  this is because again that's what  happened in jane foster in the comics  that once she died and passed on that  she went into valhalla and then became a  valkyrie and so that's really where  she's been ever since in fact she has  her own comic book run called valkyrie  which isn't terrible uh it's kind of  cool actually to be to be honest with  you guys but with that being said guys  uh that's everything we spotted right  let us know all the things that that we  may have missed down in the comments  section thank you all for watching and i  will catch you all later  peace
 

